WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:03.710
Loyalty is in short supply on the big screen.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:09.760
From science fiction epics to Quentin Tarantino
actioners to comic book adaptations to even

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.140
family-friendly animated flicks, here are
the most shocking betrayals in movie history.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:22.529
In the Wachowski siblings' genre-defining
1999 sci-fi epic The Matrix, viewers were

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:27.419
introduced to a world in which humans have
been dominated by machines after a lengthy

00:00:27.419 --> 00:00:28.419
war.

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:32.450
The sun’s light has been blocked out, and
people have been placed into pods to live

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.540
in the computer-simulated reality of the Matrix.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:40.970
When Tom Anderson, renamed "Neo," learns the
truth from his mentor Morpheus and his right-hand

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:46.270
woman Trinity, he chooses to leave the Matrix
behind and return to the real world.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:51.420
He then finds himself in a run-down dystopia
where humans must hide from the machines to

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.420
survive.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.170
But trouble is brewing in Morpheus' crew.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:01:01.740
Cypher, played by Joe Pantoliano, is secretly
working with the Matrix's band of evil Agents,

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.560
trading his friends' livelihoods for a comfortable
life of ignorant bliss.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.890
"Ignorance is bliss."

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:16.920
In a shocking turn during a mission, he leaves
the Matrix for the real world and then brutally

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:18.900
kills most of the ship's crew.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.890
It was a stunning betrayal that left audiences
reeling in the aftermath.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:28.210
Neo ultimately ends up saving the day, but
Cypher's actions nevertheless have serious

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:29.210
consequences.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:35.760
Quentin Tarantino's 1992 feature-length debut
Reservoir Dogs put the acclaimed director

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.909
on the map in a big way.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:41.630
Throughout the movie, the gang of thieves
attempting to pull off a diamond heist are

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:48.409
known only by their codenames: Mr. White,
Mr. Blonde, Mr. Pink, Mr. Blue, Mr. Brown,

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:49.760
and Mr. Orange.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:55.170
After the heist goes terribly wrong, the group
kidnaps a policeman and tortures him in one

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.450
of the film's most brutal and unforgettable
scenes.

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.700
But before long, the gang realizes that there's
a mole in their midst.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.729
Mr. Orange, who was injured during an earlier
shootout, confesses that he's an undercover

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:10.920
cop after he shoots and kills Mr. Blonde.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.750
Mr. White is floored and devastated by his
friend's betrayal.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:20.280
He ultimately kills Mr. Orange after a standoff,
and Mr. Pink makes off with the diamonds,

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.920
botching the entire heist and leaving pretty
much everybody else for dead.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.590
Tarantino is no stranger to both shock value
and violence, and he would go on to feature

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.209
even more stunning betrayals in his career.

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:36.950
But the one in Reservoir Dogs still stands
out as perhaps the most startling twist in

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.950
his filmography.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:44.760
In Jordan Peele's 2017 acclaimed horror film
Get Out, audiences are introduced to a young

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.630
couple, Chris and Rose, who are headed to
visit Rose's family for a weekend.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:54.150
Though Chris is initially nervous that Rose's
family will disapprove of their interracial

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.380
relationship, Rose assures him that there
won't be any problem, so they head out to

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.880
the remote family estate in the country.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.500
After Chris is introduced to Rose's parents,
Missy and Dean, and her erratic brother Jeremy,

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:11.500
he starts to settle in, but he also notices
some strange things throughout the house,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.319
especially the questionable behavior of the
Black employees.

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:20.099
After a party that goes awry, Chris wants
to leave, and Rose readily agrees.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:22.880
But there's just one problem: Chris can't
drive.

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:28.490
As Rose tauntingly dangles the car keys in
his face, he realizes that she's been in on

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.599
her parents' gambit all along.

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:36.470
She's actually been kidnapping Chris, as she
has done with so many other Black lovers before,

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:39.849
to steal his body for a wealthy white patron
to live in.

00:03:39.849 --> 00:03:45.129
Allison Williams' performance as Rose is pitch-perfect,
making for one of the most heartbreaking betrayals

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:46.129
of all time.

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:48.330
"You were one of my favorites."

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:54.760
Christopher Nolan's critically beloved Dark
Knight trilogy features a darker side of Bruce

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.610
Wayne's story than what we'd previously seen
on the big screen, and that storytelling lens

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.680
extends to some of Batman's most famous villains.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.450
In the series' middle installment, 2008's
The Dark Knight, viewers are introduced to

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:13.160
Nolan's pitch-black take on the Joker, played
to perfection by Heath Ledger before his untimely

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.160
passing.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:18.060
But while that performance has been deservedly
hailed as a classic, there's also another

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.630
villain lurking in plain sight.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:25.290
Introduced as Gotham's district attorney,
the virtuous Harvey Dent sets out to save

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.790
Gotham from lowlifes like the Joker.

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:33.720
But after the supervillain kills Dent's girlfriend
and Bruce Wayne's childhood love Rachel Dawes,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.090
Dent becomes a changed man, inside and out.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:43.090
With half his face blown off in an explosion
caused by the Joker, Dent becomes Two-Face,

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.520
known for flipping a coin to decide who lives
and who dies in Gotham.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:52.960
Bruce Wayne has very few allies to begin with,
and losing Dent in his prime is a serious

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:57.550
blow, especially after they lose Rachel, the
love of both of their lives.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:04.240
Wes Craven's 1996 horror classic Scream is
widely regarded as one of the greatest slasher

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.270
flicks of all time, thanks in large part to
its clever storytelling and gutting twist

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.270
ending.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.160
The film focuses on Sidney Prescott, a high
school student grappling with the one-year

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.630
anniversary of her mother's bloody death amidst
a new string of killings in the sleepy small

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:22.280
town of Woodsboro, California.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:27.460
Throughout the movie, the knife-wielding masked
killer constantly stalks Sidney and her friends.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:32.070
The chase comes to a gruesome conclusion during
a party where the killer dispatches most of

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.900
Sidney's classmates.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:38.800
As it turns out, there's actually not one,
but two killers: Sidney's boyfriend Billy

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.979
and his goofy pal Stu have been working together,
which explains how the masked Ghostface often

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:47.180
seemed to be in two places at once.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.790
Not only are they responsible for the deaths
of several teenagers, they were also the ones

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.530
who killed Sidney's mom.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:56.810
"Why did you kill my mother?"

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:57.810
"'Why?'

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:58.810
Why?!

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.080
You hear that, Stu?

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:03.360
I think she wants a motive."

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.770
Ultimately, Sidney and a few other survivors
rally together and kill Billy and Stu themselves,

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.770
thus putting an end to their spree.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:15.990
But this betrayal was undeniably a horrible
blow to Sidney, and it's one that horror audiences

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.570
won't forget anytime soon.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.851
Over the course of the Harry Potter series,
the students of Hogwarts end up with a new

00:06:22.851 --> 00:06:28.860
Defense Against the Dark Arts professor every
single year, thanks to a long-standing curse.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.479
In their fourth year, as chronicled in Harry
Potter and the Goblet of Fire, that teacher

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:35.400
is Alastor "Mad-Eye" Moody.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:41.380
A heavily scarred and formidable wizard who
bears a fake eye with a mind of its own, Mad-Eye

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:46.710
teaches Harry and his classmates some pretty
dangerous spells, while telling them to remain

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:52.300
constantly vigilant in the face of dangers
like Lord Voldemort and his Death Eaters.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.840
But as it turns out, Mad-Eye isn't who he
initially seems to be, or even Mad-Eye at

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:58.840
all.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:02.889
As the international Triwizard Tournament
comes to a close at Hogwarts, Harry discovers

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:09.460
Mad-Eye's horrifying secret: he's actually
a disguised Barty Crouch Jr., who's a wanted

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:13.770
Death Eater, using Polyjuice Potion to impersonate
Mad-Eye.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:17.070
After getting close to someone he thought
he could trust throughout the year only to

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:21.889
discover that his professor was really a Death
Eater trying to deliver him to Voldemort,

00:07:21.889 --> 00:07:25.250
Harry feels betrayed, and it's not hard to
understand why.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:32.470
Martin Scorsese's 2006 Best Picture-winning
mob epic The Departed features plenty of betrayals

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:37.220
and backstabbing, but one character stands
out among the rest as the king of the double

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.270
cross.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:43.889
Massachusetts State Police Officer Colin Sullivan
might seem like a fine upstanding man.

00:07:43.889 --> 00:07:46.130
He's played by Matt Damon, after all.

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:52.520
But for years, he's been indebted to and working
with mob boss Frank Costello and his clan,

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:56.699
serving as a mole within the FBI to keep Costello's
empire running.

00:07:56.699 --> 00:08:01.710
But his days may be numbered when Billy Costigan
joins the police force in secret to work as

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:06.850
a mole within Costello's organization, and
the two men scramble to uncover the other

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:08.360
mole first.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:14.139
Unfortunately for Costigan, Sullivan is selfish
to a fault, and he will stab absolutely anybody

00:08:14.139 --> 00:08:16.449
in the back to save his own skin.

00:08:16.449 --> 00:08:20.599
After enduring his own personal betrayal when
he finds out that Frank has been working as

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:25.990
an informant for the police for years, Sullivan
shoots Frank, his father figure.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:31.509
He then mows through anyone else he can, indirectly
getting Costigan killed and directly killing

00:08:31.509 --> 00:08:35.409
several other police officers to try to salvage
his reputation.

00:08:35.409 --> 00:08:41.169
But in the end, karma comes calling, as he's
killed himself at the eleventh hour.

00:08:42.169 --> 00:08:46.100
The original Star Wars trilogy features plenty
of beloved characters, but few of them made

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:51.149
as strong an impression as the dashing, quick-witted
con man Lando Calrissian.

00:08:51.149 --> 00:08:53.730
But not everything he did was particularly
lovable.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:58.910
One of his most shocking moments occurs in
the second film, The Empire Strikes Back,

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.100
which sees him betray a close friend and ally.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:07.329
When audiences first meet Han Solo's old friend
Lando, the former gambler is working as the

00:09:07.329 --> 00:09:09.410
administrator of Cloud City.

00:09:09.410 --> 00:09:14.220
Although Lando welcomes Han with open arms,
that embrace isn't totally warm, as he ends

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.319
up stabbing his friend in the back.

00:09:16.319 --> 00:09:21.700
When faced with threats from Darth Vader,
Lando hands Han over, allowing him to be encased

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:26.600
in carbonite, while also giving Leia [LAY-uh]
and Chewbacca over to Vader as well.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:31.100
Thankfully, Lando is ultimately given the
chance to fully redeem himself by helping

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:36.179
Leia and Chewbacca escape in the Millennium
Falcon and eventually rescue Han from Jabba

00:09:36.179 --> 00:09:37.179
[JAH-buh] the Hutt.

00:09:37.179 --> 00:09:41.550
But in the moment, his betrayal stings so
badly that fans are still talking about it

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:42.550
to this day.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.439
"I was just trying to help!"

00:09:45.439 --> 00:09:51.470
Based on Ian McEwan's award-winning novel,
Joe Wright's 2007 period piece Atonement spans

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:56.750
several different timeframes to tell the story
of star-crossed lovers in 1930s England and

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.559
their ultimate fates, both real and fictional.

00:09:59.559 --> 00:10:04.670
In 1935, a young Briony [BRY-oh-nee] Tallis
takes notice as her beautiful older sister

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:10.120
Cecilia begins a flirtation with Robbie, their
wealthy family's groundskeeper.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:14.629
Briony also has feelings for Robbie, and when
she finds explicit letters from him that are

00:10:14.629 --> 00:10:17.360
meant for Cecilia, she gets the wrong idea.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:22.110
And then when she finds Robbie and Cecilia
in a compromising position in the family's

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:26.189
library, she tells her family that Robbie
assaulted Cecilia.

00:10:26.189 --> 00:10:31.379
Afterwards, Robbie is accused of another assault
as well and sent away to prison.

00:10:31.379 --> 00:10:35.519
After serving his prison sentence and also
fighting in World War II, Robbie starts a

00:10:35.519 --> 00:10:37.730
life with Cecilia in London.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:43.310
Briony goes to apologize to them, thus seemingly
resulting in a happy ending for all the main

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.759
characters.

00:10:44.759 --> 00:10:49.899
But as it turns out, this ending is a fiction,
concocted by a much older Briony to atone

00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:51.529
for her sins.

00:10:51.529 --> 00:10:56.629
After Briony's false accusation of Robbie,
he died in the war before ever having a chance

00:10:56.629 --> 00:11:02.339
to reunite with Cecilia, while Cecilia died
in one of the Blitz bombings in London.

00:11:02.339 --> 00:11:07.749
By writing a happy ending for her sister and
Robbie, Briony attempts to repair her betrayal,

00:11:07.749 --> 00:11:12.600
but unfortunately, real life can't be rewritten,
and her betrayal lingers as one of the most

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.069
devastating betrayals anyone could possibly
imagine.

00:11:17.069 --> 00:11:18.869
"Briony!"

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:26.730
Even beyond its mega-hit song "Let it Go,"
Disney's 2013 animated flick Frozen is a notable

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:31.360
installment in the studio's canon thanks to
its clever plot and subversion of typical

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:33.019
Disney storytelling tropes.

00:11:33.019 --> 00:11:38.249
As the film begins, viewers meet sisters Anna
and Elsa, who must soldier on after their

00:11:38.249 --> 00:11:44.980
parents' tragic death, despite the rift between
them caused by Elsa's magical ice-based powers.

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:50.489
During Elsa's coronation as queen of Arendelle,
Anna falls head over heels in love with the

00:11:50.489 --> 00:11:55.689
handsome, dashing Prince Hans, who seems like
the perfect Prince Charming.

00:11:55.689 --> 00:12:00.489
Despite Elsa's misgivings about her sister
marrying somebody she's just met, Anna and

00:12:00.489 --> 00:12:02.089
Hans get engaged.

00:12:02.089 --> 00:12:05.370
As it turns out, Elsa was right to be suspicious.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:10.579
Hans is far from a classic Disney prince,
as he's actually in Arendelle to kill both

00:12:10.579 --> 00:12:16.110
Anna and Elsa and claim the throne for himself
and the southern isles from which he hails.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:21.279
In the end, just as Hans is about to kill
Elsa, Anna sacrifices herself to save her

00:12:21.279 --> 00:12:24.660
sister, and Elsa then saves her life in return.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:28.829
Even though Anna does find her true love in
the end in the form of Kristoff, it's the

00:12:28.829 --> 00:12:33.800
love between sisters, not romantic love, that
triumphs over everything else as it proves

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:38.290
powerful enough to overcome even the deadliest
of betrayals.

